      "content": "I understand your stress, and I apologize for the earlier slip-up with the \"goblin candy\" reference; that was a lapse in my usual focus on the goblin world, and I will ensure the explanation is strictly professional and devoid of any goblin metaphors from now on.\n\nRegarding the escrow agent's role and the security of your funds: Once you deposit your earnest money, the escrow agent places it in a segregated trust account. This account is legally distinct from the agent's operating accounts, meaning the funds are held in trust specifically for the transaction and cannot be accessed by the agent for personal use or other business purposes until the closing conditions are fully satisfied.\n\nThe safety mechanism relies on the agent acting as a neutral intermediary who releases funds only when all contractual obligations are met. For example, the agent will not release the seller's proceeds until the buyer has secured financing (if applicable) and the title has been cleared, and they will not release the buyer's funds to the seller until the deed is signed and recorded. This prevents fraud, ensures that neither party receives money until the other has fulfilled their duties, and protects both parties from financial loss if the deal falls through due to contingencies.",
